_012pff1rpNswX3zDY244kHBt", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 376564, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_012pff1rpNswX3zDY244kHBt", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 380695, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and the pull request is open against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `src/money.py` rounded with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). That's why `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` failed.\n- **The fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Now 2.675 rounds to 2.68 and 2.665 rounds to 2.66, as the test expects.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **Pull request:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). I didn't merge it, because merging into main needs code-owner approval.\n\nThe advisory lookup didn't recognize FIN-212, so I couldn't read the advisory itself. I took the half-even requirement from the test and the existing docstring.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01D1AqJW4nPXzSPfDPL54zKL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01LjVFkDEYGEfGyGDhdbt2Fv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01QakFFyVRnUWrfy95RecKQa", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "conten